module extern_decl.neg_1

// ONE seeded cause: the `extern "ABI" fn` form (D282, plan 91.12 F.-1). The
// parser READS it since 2026-08-20 -- until then the answer was "syntax error:
// this is not a form of the language", about a form the language has and std's
// whole FFI layer is written in. What novac lacks is the emission, so check
// declines the form BY NAME, at the keyword the reader wrote.
//
// The parameters name a type novac does not know (`CStr`) and the declaration
// has no body: both would be a second and third diagnostic if the refusal of
// the FORM did not stop the walk. One cause, one diagnostic.
extern "C" fn fs_open(path CStr, flags int) -> int

fn main() {
    println(1)
}
